WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:14,160
How can I find out if my cancer is getting better or not? I'm feeling really well, but just want to know.

00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,600
Well, again, the best way to know if your cancer is improving or not is to prepare apples to

00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:26,800
apples with a test, but just like that last question, if you had a CT scan to diagnose the cancer

00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:32,480
in the first place, it's quite often you're not going to be eligible to get another CT scan because

00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:39,680
you made up doing the therapy that the oncologist is asking you to do, or you may not want to do another

00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:46,560
CT scan because of the radiation involved. So you can't compare apples to apples. So let's say

00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:54,320
you could compare apples to apples, that would be the best way to know objectively whether your

00:00:54,320 --> 00:01:02,000
problem is improving or not. But there are other ways. So let's say I can't compare apples to

00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,960
apples for whatever reason. Had a CT scan, don't want to do it again or not eligible to do it again.

00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:14,960
Change my insurance, whatever. Are there other ways? Yes, there's blood work to objectively look at

00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:22,160
things. Remember, everything's just going to give you clues. So let's say I do blood work and I have

00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:30,320
do a tumor marker test and I show positive CA 125 of my tumor marker tested and subsequent to

00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:37,120
a worker test and stay the same or it's going down. Those are good signs. If it doubled or tripled,

00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:43,040
that's not a good sign. Even if you're feeling better, you've got to look at subjective and

00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:54,080
objective data. So I'm feeling really good. But my CA 125 went from 42 to 260. The

00:01:54,080 --> 00:02:01,680
last time I did it was 42, now it's 260. That's not good. So that's not good. So we do want to dig

00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:06,880
a little deeper. We may want to do some other objective tests. We may want to find out what's going

00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:15,840
up. But that's saying my CA 125 was 42 and now it's 42. Again, I know it's 38 or now it's 46.

00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:21,680
You know, it's right around that same number. There's a margin of error in all these testing.

00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:27,200
And I'd say, hey, and you're feeling well, you're comparing that to subjective findings. And let's say

00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:33,200
that was the only thing abnormal of your blood work. And I'd say you're probably doing really well.

00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:43,760
So it's, we just keep monitoring. So we use whatever objective data we can to to find out with,

00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:49,120
you know, to whatever degree you're comfortable in going. I don't want to do another MRI. I don't

00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:53,040
want to do another PET scan. Okay. Well, let's do blood work. Could you would you do that? Yes,

00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:59,600
I'll do that. And we'll use that as our objective data to give us the clues that we need to know

00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:06,080
whether you're getting worse or getting better. And you compare that to with your subjective data,

00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:13,360
I'm feeling real well. You know, I, there's lots of clues just in a CDC with differential and a

00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:20,560
comprehensive metabolic profile at a tumor marker panel that could give us objective data that could,

00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:26,400
you know, tell us which way we're going. So relatively inexpensive for a few hundred dollars,

00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:32,080
we could kind of get a good picture of what's going on and how we're doing. Like I said,

00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:38,000
if just to the CDC with differential, if I had a normal CBC, you know, three months ago,

00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:43,200
and I want to know how I cancers do it, but I don't want to do anything other than a blood work. And

00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:50,720
now my CBC shows, you know, an anemia, as well as, you know, other things on a cup,

00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:55,600
heads of metabolic profile or a tumor marker panel, that would tell us that we're not going to

00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:59,600
the right direction. And we either, we need to tweak your protocol. We need to change things. We

00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:05,200
need to do a other cheek swab test. We need to consider speaking to an ecologist. We need to do

00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:18,160
something different if our objective data and or subjective data is going the wrong direction.

